# Static-host routing (Netlify / Cloudflare Pages read this file from the publish root).
#
# The console owns /login when co-hosted via `vital serve --site`. On a static
# deploy nothing answers that path, so serve the sign-in landing page instead of
# a 404. Keep the URL as /login so the links in index.html stay unchanged.
# (login/index.html already resolves as a directory index on every static host —
# this rule just skips the extra 301 hop.)
/login    /login/index.html   200

# One canonical entry point.
/index.html   /   301
